# =============================================================================
# Argus-Trader — .gitignore
#
# Standard: docs/git-hardening-guidelines.md §6.2 (exclude secrets by pattern,
# not by filename) and §6.3 (name the data class and the reason, so the file
# records the decision and not just the effect).
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. Git history is not a delete-capable store: a
# credential that is pushed must be rotated, not removed. Everything in the
# first section is therefore excluded by pattern, so a file nobody anticipated
# is still caught by shape.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored — the Phase 1 design (§11) tracks these in git:
#   data/raw/polygon/       quarterly Parquet partitions, sized to stay under
#                           GitHub's per-file limit precisely so they can be
#                           committed
#   data/*.json             order and position state, the audit ledger
#   artifacts/agents_data/  the daily serialized agent outputs
#   test_results/           the performance baseline the CI regression gate
#                           compares candidates against
#   docs/index.html         the dashboard the publish step commits and Pages
#                           serves
# If that changes, change it here and in the design document together.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
#
# Argus-Trader depends on two paid, keyed services — Polygon.io for market data
# and the LLM provider behind the Tier 2 committee — so a leak here costs money
# as well as access. Patterns, not names, for the reason above.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
*.crt
*.pfx
*.p12
*.token
*secrets*
*credentials*
credentials.json
client_secret*.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch and personal data
#
# Brokerage statements, account exports and real position files are used
# locally during development and must never reach a public repository. They go
# under local/, which is excluded wholesale so no individual filename has to be
# anticipated.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
local/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python environments and bytecode
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test, lint and coverage artifacts
#
# Backtest runs under test_results/{DATE}_PR-{ID}_{SHA}/ are committed on
# purpose (design §10) — these are the tool caches around them, which are not.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime logs and process state
#
# The daily batch writes logs and pid files next to the code it runs; neither
# belongs in a diff.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
*.pid

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, agent and OS noise
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
